course: dictionary
lesson: 8587
title: Scissors: a tool and a movement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scissors is a plural word, so we talk about a pair of scissors, just as we say a pair of socks. The tool has two blades joined in the middle, and you open and close them with your fingers. «Use child scissors, carry them closed and pointing down, and pass them handle first.»
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is right. In art lessons, scissors cut paper, card and string. In a sports lesson, a scissor kick means your legs cross over each other like the blades of scissors. Read the sentence around the word to decide.
explain: Safety words matter too. Walk with scissors pointed down, pass them handle first, cut away from your body, and never run with them. «A see-saw, scissors, a bottle opener and a wheelbarrow all use levers.» Scissors work like levers: pressing the handles moves the blades together to cut.
fact: Scissors is a noun, and we usually use it in the plural: a pair of scissors.
fact: «Scissors» means a cutting tool with two blades joined in the middle.
fact: A scissor kick or scissor movement is when the legs cross like scissor blades.
fact: Safety scissors and child scissors are made to be safer for children to use.
fact: Children do not cut their own hair, because scissors near the eyes are dangerous.
exercise: «Use child scissors, carry them closed and pointing down, and pass them handle first.» How should you pass scissors to a friend? | Blades first | Open, with the points up | *Handle first | Thrown across the table
exercise: A footballer does a scissor kick. What does scissor mean in this sentence? | A pair of socks | Hair cut very short | A tool for cutting paper | *Legs crossing over each other like scissor blades
exercise: Which of these is a safe way to carry scissors? | Open, with the points aimed at a friend | Waving them above your head | *Closed, with the points down | Running down the corridor
test: Which phrase is the correct way to talk about one scissors tool? | Scissor blades only | A scissors | A scissor | *A pair of scissors
test: Why do children not cut their own hair? | Hair is too soft to cut | Scissors only work on paper | Scissors are too heavy for small hands | *It often goes wrong, and scissors near the eyes are dangerous
exam: What does «scissors» mean in «Pass the scissors to me, handle first»? | A kind of hair clip | A scissor kick in football | *A cutting tool with two blades | A pair of socks
